==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Prof. Cat Jobs''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Headmaster Cat Jobs''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
It's always worth bringing Prof. Cat Jobs for the [[Good Jobs! (Combo)|Good Jobs!]] [[Cat Combo|Combo]] in [[:Category:XP Guerrilla Stages|XP stages]] and easy stages overall, but he can also be useful in his own right as a support unit. He may be useless in cases where there are enemies that can hit past the frontline (such as [[Kory]] with his [[Wave Attack|Waves]]), and he cannot take on hordes, but he can nullify almost all damage from single, mid-low-ranged bosses, such as [[Teacher Bun Bun]], [[Bore]], [[R.Ost]] and other strong pushers whose range is less than his, as long as he is protected and helped in making sure to hit the right enemy, reducing alot of stresses of holding back said enemies. The downside is that you'll have to fight them close to the [[Cat Base]], as waiting for him to inch his way towards the enemy base may take longer than just killing them outright.

He is very useful against [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, as he can outrange nearly all of them and cripple their damage, making it harder for them to break through your units. This is most useful for [[Primeval Cyclone]], which has fairly low damage but has few accessible counters. Similarly, he can also be used to stall [[Big Sal]] and [[Miss Haka]] at the Cat Base in a pinch if needed and buy some valuable time.

==='''True Form'''===
Headmaster Cat Jobs' [[Surge Attack]] can, in part, solve the Single Attack problem, as all enemy units that enter it will be weakened. The Surge also has a chance to snipe backliners, as it can reach all the way to 1,050 range. However, the unreliability of this huge spawn area makes for a double-edged sword unless stacked; sooner or later, one of the Surges will spawn away from what it should be hitting, giving the enemies a chance to start pushing again.

His extra movement speed and ability to survive a lethal strike allow Cat Jobs bring him from a gimmick unit that's impractical outside of some odd scenarios to a useful cat that can genuinely help on many stages, as he is more likely to reach the enemy in time, even entering the range of the likes of [[THE SLOTH]] to possibly weaken them in time, in addition to being able to last twice as long on the battlefield.

He can be stacked on stages with [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies or [[:Category:Enemies with Barriers|enemies with Barriers]] to make the Surges reliably hit both the frontlines and backlines, but this is generally a risky strategy due to his fairly low range, slow speed and long cooldown.

