==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Freshman Cat Jobs was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Reinforcements (Removed Combo)|Reinforcements]].
*Prior to [[Version 14.1 Update|Version 14.1]], [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]], [[Rich Cat III (Super Rare Cat)|Rich Cat III]] and Freshman Cat Jobs could only be unlocked when "Reinforcements" was part of the current pool.
*His descriptions refer to the real-life Harvard University & Nobel Prize.
*Excluding immobile cats (such as the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall Cat]]), Freshman Cat Jobs is tied with [[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Mighty Kristul Muu]] and [[Li'l Clops Cat Egg (Special Cat)|Li'l Clops Cat Egg]] for being the slowest cat in the game.
*Freshman Cat Jobs made a cameo on the Study upgrade's icon before he was added to the game.
*Prof. Cat Jobs is the only cat in the game to have a Study Power UP [[Cat Combo]], that being [[Good Jobs! (Combo)|Good Jobs!]].
*Freshman Cat Jobs is tied with [[Elder Flame Doron]] and the [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou|PC exclusive]] unit [[Natsu Mikan (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Natsu Mikan]] for the strongest weaken of any character in the game, reducing unit damage to 1% of what it was originally.
*Due to rounding and his ability's very low weaken percentage, enemies with weak attacks may be unable to deal any damage to their targets (some units may need the Resistant/Insanely Tough ability to reduce that damage even further). This results in the "damage dealt" sound not playing, similarly to when Dodge Attack is active. As a result, even units that have activated their Survive ability can withstand any number of such hits, despite having only one health point remaining. This is easy to note on [[Kang Roo]], as her second hit is very weak, dealing less than 50 damage even in [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3 and is therefore nullified by rounding.
*The word ''Okamehachimoku'' in Freshman Cat Jobs' Japanese name, Okamehachimoku Cat, means "bystander's vantage point": the idea that a person observing a game or other such scenario can judge each move better than those participating.
*Prof. Cat Jobs' Japanese name, Dr. Okamenomizu, is a reference to [[wikia:astroboy:Hiroshi Ochanomizu|Hiroshi Ochanomizu]], an ''Astro Boy'' character who also has white curly hair and is often depicted in a white suit with four buttons.

